      walkthrough = "**Level:** 100\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis task starts with Ghrald McMannus in Katta Castellum. He can be found at /way -301, 150, 69 in the big castle in the northwest section of the zone, up on the 2nd floor in one of the rooms on the south side.\nYou say, 'Hail, Ghrald McMannus'\nGhrald McMannus says, 'Thank you for your diligence in finding us. I don't think I told you that before.' He lets out a hearty sigh and looks with concern over towards Gaius. 'I am at the whims of Gaius' flights of fancy, in hopes that one might lead us to the answer, yet I protect him from anything that may harm him in our [pursuit].'\nYou say, 'What is your pursuit?'\nGhrald McMannus says, 'I mentioned before that I think this may be the work of the gods, or a god, but we need some information to try to narrow it down. Whether they have made themselves known to Gaius, he hasn't stated, but I have some potential [sources] of knowledge we can research.'\nYou say, 'What sources are you looking into?'\nGhrald McMannus says, 'There are some books regarding visions of various types and the madness that can accompany them. Frankly our history is wrought with examples of various gods affecting fragile mortal minds. A simple touch can do so much to you or me. Would you mind trying to [gather] these books for our research?'\nYou say, 'I will gather the books.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Chasing Madness'.\nGhrald McMannus says, 'Excellent. I appreciate your attention to this. There are two books in particular to look for. One is in the possession of an old acquaintance of mine, Rusbek, in the Misty Thicket. If you give his pups a bite to eat, he might let you know where to find it. He might not entertain giving it up otherwise, and for that I apologize in advance. The other book is one I had been reading in the New Tanaan library. When word came of Gaius' condition, I left rather swiftly, so it was left on one of the tables. It may still be there if no one's restored it back to its shelf.'\nGhrald McMannus' friend Gaius Ludanus, an adherent to Drinal the Silver Reaper, has fallen mad under some visions that have started to make themselves known to everyone around them. So far, no one has been hurt but many have gone mad in the process of his travels and in the presence of the small baby dragons that have started popping up in the realms of Norrath and Ludin.\nGhrald indicated that giving some treats to Rusbek's wolves should allow you to gain Rusbek's trust to get your hands on the book he is in the possession of. Ghrald informed you that the book he's looking for in the New Tanaan library should be on a table there if it hadn't been put back.\n- 1. Give one of Rusbek's Wolves a delicious treat 0/1 Misty Thicket\nGo to Misty Thicket. You can find Rusbek the Inhospitable. He is in the southeaster corner of the zone near a couple of cottages with his 2 wolves. Give one of his wolves any food, I don't think it matters what it is as long as it is food.\nYou offered 1 Iron Ration to Cozy.\nRusbek the Inhospitable says, 'Well, that's kind of you, I guess. I'm guessing you're here to sweeten us up for the book? It's inside, in the back. Just, uh, make sure our mutual friend keeps HIS friend away from Misty Thicket.'\nYour task 'Chasing Madness' has been updated.\nYou complete the trade with Cozy.\n- 2. Head into Rusbek's cottage to get the book When Obsessions Turn to Madness 0/1 Misty Thicket\nQuest Text: Rusbek has indicated the book you're looking for is inside his house. Ghrald informed you that the book he's looking for in the New Tannan library should be on a table there is it hadn't been put back.\nGo into the cottage that Rusbek is standing in front of. One the dresser is an open book, click on it to loot When Obssessions Turn to Madness.\nYour task 'Chasing Madness' has been updated.\n- 3. Pick up the book From Madness Comes Clarity in the New Tannan library 0/1 The Plane of Knowledge\nQuest Text: Ghrald informed that the book he's looking for in the New Tannan library should be on a table there if it hadn't been put back. With the book When Obsessions Turn to Madness now in your possession, it's time to take it to Ghrald McMannus.\nThe book is located on the table at /way -105, 836, 74 in the library next to Tomeseeker Salkien, near where the Ranger spells are sold, at the base of the stairs going to the next floor. It's the smaller book by itself and not in the stacked books.\nYour task 'Chasing Madness' has been updated.\n- 4. Give When Obsessions Turn to Madness to Ghrald McMannus 0/1 Katta Castellum\nQuest Text: With the book When Obsessions Turn to Madness now in your possession, its time to take it to Ghrald McMannus. With the book From Madness Comes Clarity now in your possession, its time to talk it to Ghrald McMannus.\nYou offered 1 When Obsessions Turn to Madness to Ghrald McMannus.\nYour task 'Chasing Madness' has been updated.\nGhrald McMannus says, 'Ah, I will have to thank Rusbek later for taking good care of this text.'\nYou complete the trade with Ghrald McMannus.\n- 5. Give From Madness Comes Clarity to Ghrald McMannus 0/1 Katta Castellum\nYou offered 1 From Madness Comes Clarity to Ghrald McMannus.\nYour task 'Chasing Madness' has been updated.\nGhrald McMannus says, 'You found it! With so many books in the Library, I worried it might have been a tough find.'\nYou complete the trade with Ghrald McMannus.\n- 6. Check In with Ghrald McMannus 0/1 Katta Castellum\nYou say, 'Hail, Ghrald McMannus'\nGhrald McMannus skims through the text of the first book, then swiftly flips the other book on top to cross-reference some of the data. 'I'm afraid I have a lot to ingest here. I do have some [requests] to see if we can fill in some blanks.'\nYou say, 'What requests are those?'\nGhrald McMannus says, 'I'd like for you to reach out to a few planar representatives of gods who may be involved. First, a Priest of Terris Thule in the Plane of Nightmare. From there, a Priest of Saryrn in the Plane of Torment. If you still can't find exactly what you're looking for, seek a Priest of Ayonae Ro in what was once the Plane of Music. [And then]...'\nYou say, 'And then?'\nYour task 'Chasing Madness' has been updated.\nGhrald McMannus says, 'Zebuxoruk wishes for no worshippers, so finding one, even a priest, may be difficult. You may have better luck seeking the Ungod out directly, if you can figure out WHEN to seek him out...'\n- 7. Speak with a Priest of Nightmares in the Plane of Nightmare 0/1 The Plane Nightmare\nQuest Text: Speak with a Priest of Terris-Thule's in the Plane of Nightmare for any information as to this mystery.\nPriest of Nightmares [npc=59879] is located at -1351, -1350, 124 in the far southeastern section of the zone in the graveyard in the middle building. He's on Find (Ctrl+F).\nBe ready for this step, it spawns a mad nightmare [npc=59882] that attacks. it's fairly weak (level 106) for players 120+. About 6 million hp and doesn't hit for very much. It drops an item, give it to all in the group in the task.\nYou say, 'Hail, Priest of Nightmares'\nPriest of Nightmares says, 'Quiet. I am trying to [sleep].'\nYou say, 'You are trying to sleep standing up?'\nPriest of Nightmares says, 'It's the best way to ensure I fall to the ground to wake myself from the nightmare. It's a beautiful and terrifying [cycle].'\nYou say, 'Why the cycle?'\nPriest of Nightmares says, 'Some of the delicious terror is in trying to go back to sleep with those nightmarish [visions] freshly intruding into your mind. Will you find yourself in the same horrifying situations, or will more seek to disrupt your hours of rest?'\nYou say, 'I've come to find a priest about visions.'\nPriest of Nightmares says, 'Do you also want to sleep in horror? Do you want to [see things] that will scare your very soul?'\nYou say, 'It's for a friend. They see things